Updated recommendation based on your sizes (vector length 500–3000, P ≈ 50 or less):

A pure fully-connected network on such long vectors becomes
inefficient (too many parameters, slow, prone to overfitting). A
hybrid architecture works much better:

Process the small P (parameters) with fully connected layers.
Process the long X (initial vector) with 1D convolutions.
Combine the two branches and predict the output vector Y.

This is efficient and effective for your variable X–Y differences.

%% Data prep
% Shapes:
% P: [numParams x N]     ≈ 50 x N
% X: [vecLen x N]        500–3000 x N
% Y: [vecLen x N]        target

% Normalize separately (recommended)
[Pnorm, muP, sigP] = normalize(P, 2);
[Xnorm, muX, sigX] = normalize(X, 2);
[Ynorm, muY, sigY] = normalize(Y, 2);

InputP = Pnorm;
InputX = Xnorm;   % keep separate for hybrid network
Target = Ynorm;

%% Define hybrid network (dlnetwork)
vecLen = size(X, 1);
numParams = size(P, 1);

% --- Branch for small parameters P ---
pBranch = [
    featureInputLayer(numParams, 'Name','pInput')
    fullyConnectedLayer(64, 'Name','pFC1')
    reluLayer
    fullyConnectedLayer(128, 'Name','pFC2')
    reluLayer
];

% --- Branch for long vector X (1D Conv) ---
xBranch = [
    sequenceInputLayer(1, 'Name','xInput')   % 1 channel
    convolution1dLayer(7, 32, 'Padding','same', 'Name','conv1')
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer
    maxPooling1dLayer(2, 'Stride',2)
    
    convolution1dLayer(5, 64, 'Padding','same')
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer
    maxPooling1dLayer(2, 'Stride',2)
    
    convolution1dLayer(5, 128, 'Padding','same')
    batchNormalizationLayer
    reluLayer
];

% --- Combine branches ---
combine = [
    concatenationLayer(1, 2, 'Name','concat')   % or depthConcatenationLayer if needed
    fullyConnectedLayer(256)
    reluLayer
    fullyConnectedLayer(vecLen)   % output same length as Y
];

% Build full layer graph
lgraph = layerGraph(pBranch);
lgraph = addLayers(lgraph, xBranch);
lgraph = addLayers(lgraph, combine);

lgraph = connectLayers(lgraph, 'pFC2', 'concat/in1');

% Connect X branch output to concat (need to flatten)
lgraph = addLayers(lgraph, fullyConnectedLayer(vecLen/4, 'Name','xFlatten')); % approximate
lgraph = connectLayers(lgraph, 'relu_3', 'xFlatten');  % adjust name
lgraph = connectLayers(lgraph, 'xFlatten', 'concat/in2');

net = dlnetwork(lgraph);

